    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19 Disclosure of interests",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-council-act-2003#sec-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-heritage-council-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-heritage-council-act-2003.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A member who has a direct or indirect pecuniary interest in a\nmatter that is being considered, or is about to be considered, by the\nCouncil must disclose the nature of the interest to the other\nmembers.\n\n(2) The disclosure must be made as soon as possible after the relevant\nfacts have come to the member’s knowledge.\n\n(3) Unless the Council otherwise determines, the member:\n\n(a) must not be present during any deliberation by the Council\non the matter; and\n\n(b) must not take part in any decision of the Council on the\nmatter.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a determination under subsection (3), the\nmember:\n\n(a) must not be present during any deliberation of the Council on\nwhether to make the determination; and\n\n(b) must not take part in making the determination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A member who has a direct or indirect pecuniary interest in a\nmatter that is being considered, or is about to be considered, by the\nCouncil must disclose the nature of the interest to the other\nmembers.\n\n(2) The disclosure must be made as soon as possible after the relevant\nfacts have come to the member’s knowledge.\n\n(3) Unless the Council otherwise determines, the member:\n\n(a) must not be present during any deliberation by the Council\non the matter; and\n\n(b) must not take part in any decision of the Council on the\nmatter.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a determination under subsection (3), the\nmember:\n\n(a) must not be present during any deliberation of the Council on\nwhether to make the determination; and\n\n(b) must not take part in making the determination.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-19-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-19-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-19-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-19-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f272e511604921e5883d7772e6ad9b3cca85af458dac910597dc6c676df5b171"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-council-act-2003#sec-19",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19 Disclosure of interests",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A member who has a direct or indirect pecuniary interest in a\nmatter that is being considered, or is about to be considered, by the\nCouncil must disclose the nature of the interest to the other\nmembers.\n\n(2) The disclosure must be made as soon as possible after the relevant\nfacts have come to the member’s knowledge.\n\n(3) Unless the Council otherwise determines, the member:\n\n(a) must not be present during any deliberation by the Council\non the matter; and\n\n(b) must not take part in any decision of the Council on the\nmatter.\n\n(4) For the purposes of a determination under subsection (3), the\nmember:\n\n(a) must not be present during any deliberation of the Council on\nwhether to make the determination; and\n\n(b) must not take part in making the determination."
    },
