      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-20a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20A Resolutions without meeting",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-council-act-2003#sec-20a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-heritage-council-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-heritage-council-act-2003.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council may pass a resolution without a Council meeting\nbeing held if a majority of the members entitled to vote on the\nresolution:\n\n(a) sign a document containing a statement that they are in\nfavour of the resolution set out in the document; or\n\n(b) otherwise indicate, in accordance with a method determined\nby the Council, that they are in favour of the resolution.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), separate copies of a\ndocument may be used for signing by the members if the wording\nof the resolution and statement is identical in each copy.\n\n(3) The resolution is passed when the last of the members signs the\ndocument or otherwise indicates that he or she is in favour of the\nresolution.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Council may pass a resolution without a Council meeting\nbeing held if a majority of the members entitled to vote on the\nresolution:\n\n(a) sign a document containing a statement that they are in\nfavour of the resolution set out in the document; or\n\n(b) otherwise indicate, in accordance with a method determined\nby the Council, that they are in favour of the resolution.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), separate copies of a\ndocument may be used for signing by the members if the wording\nof the resolution and statement is identical in each copy.\n\n(3) The resolution is passed when the last of the members signs the\ndocument or otherwise indicates that he or she is in favour of the\nresolution.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-20a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-20a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-20a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6948c37c00d6120129b21ccb18f32d3fa7c213e7103c171a248f63fa9beabd4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-council-act-2003#sec-20a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20A Resolutions without meeting",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council may pass a resolution without a Council meeting\nbeing held if a majority of the members entitled to vote on the\nresolution:\n\n(a) sign a document containing a statement that they are in\nfavour of the resolution set out in the document; or\n\n(b) otherwise indicate, in accordance with a method determined\nby the Council, that they are in favour of the resolution.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), separate copies of a\ndocument may be used for signing by the members if the wording\nof the resolution and statement is identical in each copy.\n\n(3) The resolution is passed when the last of the members signs the\ndocument or otherwise indicates that he or she is in favour of the\nresolution."
    },
