    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-24a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24A Reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-council-act-2003#sec-24a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-heritage-council-act-2003.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-heritage-council-act-2003.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council may prepare a report on any matters related to the\nfunctions of the Council and provide the report to the Minister.\n\n(2) A report prepared under subsection (1) may include the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the activities of the Council;\n\n(b) the protection and conservation of heritage;\n\n(c) how a place included in the National Heritage List or\nCommonwealth Heritage List is being managed or\nconserved;\n\n(d) the effectiveness of any measures intended to protect or\nconserve the heritage values of a place or places included in\nthe National Heritage List or Commonwealth Heritage List;\n\n(e) the provisions of grants and other financial assistance related\nto heritage;\n\n(f) policies, plans and programs of the Commonwealth or of a\nState or self-governing Territory that relate to or have an\nimpact on heritage;\n\n(g) how the National Heritage List or Commonwealth Heritage\nList are being maintained;\n\n(h) how the condition of a place included in the National\nHeritage List or Commonwealth Heritage List is being\nmonitored.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of a report provided to the\nMinister under subsection (1) to be laid before each House of the\nParliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on\nwhich the Minister receives the report.\n\n\nRegulations  Part 6\n\nSection 25\n\nAustralian Heritage Council Act 2003\nCompilation date: 1/7/19\nRegistered: 1/7/19",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Council may prepare a report on any matters related to the\nfunctions of the Council and provide the report to the Minister.\n\n(2) A report prepared under subsection (1) may include the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the activities of the Council;\n\n(b) the protection and conservation of heritage;\n\n(c) how a place included in the National Heritage List or\nCommonwealth Heritage List is being managed or\nconserved;\n\n(d) the effectiveness of any measures intended to protect or\nconserve the heritage values of a place or places included in\nthe National Heritage List or Commonwealth Heritage List;\n\n(e) the provisions of grants and other financial assistance related\nto heritage;\n\n(f) policies, plans and programs of the Commonwealth or of a\nState or self-governing Territory that relate to or have an\nimpact on heritage;\n\n(g) how the National Heritage List or Commonwealth Heritage\nList are being maintained;\n\n(h) how the condition of a place included in the National\nHeritage List or Commonwealth Heritage List is being\nmonitored.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of a report provided to the\nMinister under subsection (1) to be laid before each House of the\nParliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on\nwhich the Minister receives the report.\n\n\nRegulations  Part 6\n\nSection 25\n\nAustralian Heritage Council Act 2003\nCompilation date: 1/7/19\nRegistered: 1/7/19",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-24a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-24a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-heritage-council-act-2003-sec-24a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e1901ade320740b8475851bfa51c4030d03d76ccbecb5d62cab88fd32fb013d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-heritage-council-act-2003#sec-24a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24A Reports",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council may prepare a report on any matters related to the\nfunctions of the Council and provide the report to the Minister.\n\n(2) A report prepared under subsection (1) may include the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the activities of the Council;\n\n(b) the protection and conservation of heritage;\n\n(c) how a place included in the National Heritage List or\nCommonwealth Heritage List is being managed or\nconserved;\n\n(d) the effectiveness of any measures intended to protect or\nconserve the heritage values of a place or places included in\nthe National Heritage List or Commonwealth Heritage List;\n\n(e) the provisions of grants and other financial assistance related\nto heritage;\n\n(f) policies, plans and programs of the Commonwealth or of a\nState or self-governing Territory that relate to or have an\nimpact on heritage;\n\n(g) how the National Heritage List or Commonwealth Heritage\nList are being maintained;\n\n(h) how the condition of a place included in the National\nHeritage List or Commonwealth Heritage List is being\nmonitored.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of a report provided to the\nMinister under subsection (1) to be laid before each House of the\nParliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on\nwhich the Minister receives the report.\n\n\nRegulations  Part 6\n\nSection 25\n\nAustralian Heritage Council Act 2003\nCompilation date: 1/7/19\nRegistered: 1/7/19"
    },
